BT /F2 19 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 785 Tm (3. Introduction) Tj ET
0.25 0.45 0.65 RG 50 766 m 545 766 l S
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 751 Tm (Named Entity Recognition \(NER\) assigns a semantic label to each token in a sentence,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 737 Tm (identifying people, locations, organisations, times and other entity types. It is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 723 Tm (sequence-labelling problem used in information retrieval, search, question answering and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 709 Tm (knowledge extraction. This project compares the two approaches requested in the course) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm (guide: a classic conditional random field \(CRF\) based on handcrafted features and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 681 Tm (deep-learning systems that learn representations from data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 662 Tm (The work follows a controlled progression. Three CRFs show the effect of increasingly rich) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 648 Tm (morphology and context. A BiLSTM removes manual feature engineering but exposes overfitting,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 634 Tm (out-of-vocabulary \(OOV\) handling and independent tag decisions. GloVe embeddings address) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 620 Tm (lexical coverage, a CRF output layer models sequence transitions, their combination) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 606 Tm (addresses both issues, and DistilBERT adds contextual subword representations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.35 g 1 0 0 1 278 25 Tm (3 / 10) Tj ET

endstream
endobj
